<task id="150" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Lock sprk_issecure — field-level security so ONLY the BFF (through the secure/unsecure endpoints) changes it on project, matter and work assignment; every other writer removed; readers never masked</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; owner round 2 item 2)</phase>
    <gate>after 144 (the endpoints this task routes every secure/unsecure change through are generalized to matter and work assignment there) and 151 (both edit Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs). Not concurrently with 133 or 148 (all edit ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs / UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs — whichever lands second rebases).</gate>
    <status>completed-with-escalation</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Dataverse field-level security on an isolation flag, plus .cs and .ts/.tsx changes to the secure-create flow and a new client surface; tags bff-api, auth, security, frontend.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive platform configuration whose most likely failure is SILENT and fail-open: a field-secured flag that a caller cannot read comes back absent, and every reader treats absent as not-secure, routing secure content to a shared SPE container that cannot be retracted.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs and SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md after task 144 (133 and 148 also edit the endpoint files — not concurrently); RecordContainerResolver.cs after task 151; CreateProjectWizard.tsx / projectService.ts / SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx are shared with other wizard work; the new-environment setup step is shared with task 145.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>144, 151</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, solution, fields, frontend, fluent-ui, ribbon, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 2 item 2 (2026-09-30): "sprk_issecure is LOCKED and managed through the endpoint. Field-level security plus endpoint-only writes." Session 27 live fact: 0 fieldpermission rows cover sprk_issecure; anyone with Write can change it.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make sprk_issecure on sprk_project, sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment a field that no user and no client can write. Only the BFF's app identity, acting through the secure/unsecure endpoints, may set or clear it. Every current writer is found and moved onto the endpoint, the form control becomes read-only, users get a supported way to secure and unsecure a record through the endpoint, and every reader of the flag keeps seeing its true value.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — Dataverse field-level security, BFF ExternalAccess endpoints, and the Create Project wizard (Fluent v9). Fail closed (ADR-003); prove every live claim by an impersonated read or write.</role>

  <goal>(1) sprk_issecure is field-secured on all three roots; a field security profile grants Read to every user and Create/Update to nobody but the BFF app identity (explicitly associated, not relying on System Administrator); the platform's non-narrowable System Administrator field permission is the only other writer, and the owner has ruled on it (escalation); (2) no client code writes the flag — the Create Project wizard and the Summarize Files create-project path send "secure requested" to the BFF, which sets the flag; (3) a secure-requested create whose provisioning fails uploads nothing to a shared container; (4) the MDA form controls are read-only, and users can secure and unsecure a project, matter or work assignment through an endpoint-backed surface; (5) a non-admin user's MDA/Web API write of the flag is refused, and the same user's read of it returns the true value; (6) setup guide and pipeline carry the FLS configuration.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 THE FAILURE MODE TO DESIGN AGAINST IS READ MASKING, NOT WRITE ACCESS. Dataverse field-level security masks a secured column for any caller without a Read grant — the row comes back WITHOUT the attribute, no error. Every reader of sprk_issecure maps "absent" to "not secure":
- BFF: `Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs:211-227` — its own comment names this exact hazard ("FIELD-LEVEL SECURITY on sprk_issecure returns the row with the attribute masked out … the latter would silently route content to the shared container"). It reads through the app-only `IGenericEntityService`, so it is safe only while the app identity can read the field.
- Client, user context: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/RecordContainerResolver.ts:268-287` (`record[SECURE_FLAG_ATTRIBUTE] === true`), `src/client/pcf/TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts:934-955`.
- Any impersonated BFF read that selects the flag (the task 035/036 impersonated root sets run as the user — masking applies to them).
- BFF app-only readers of the root flags for the external plane (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs:605` `IsSecure: row.sprk_issecure == true`, `ExternalDataService.cs:1148`) — masked for the app identity, a secure root reads as not secure and the FR-22 Secure suppression is lost.
- The MDA form business rule that shows the secure section only when `sprk_issecure = true` (`src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_externalrecordaccess/views-schema.md:205`).
So "lock" means Update/Create restricted, Read granted to every user. A lock that masks reads turns a secure record into an unprotected one on every client upload path, silently and irreversibly (SPE permissions are additive-only).

THE PRECEDENT, AND ITS LESSON. This repo already field-secures one column: `contact.sprk_standinggrant` (IsSecured=TRUE, "Standing Grant Administrators" profile; recipe and live evidence in `projects/teams-app-r1/notes/050-standing-grant-field-schema.md` §2 (`:30-43`, incl. the System Administrator auto-permission at `:40`), §5 item 4 (`:85`) and its reproduction script §8 (`:106-145`)). Two facts from it bind this task: (a) marking a column IsSecured auto-creates a permission for the built-in System Administrator profile with full Read/Create/Update — so every holder of the System Administrator security role (humans AND the BFF app users, which hold it — session27 live facts) can write the flag regardless of any profile this task creates, and that profile cannot be narrowed; (b) the BFF app user's FLS Read on that column was left as an operator step and never applied, so the feature read "no standing grant" for every contact with no error (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs:168-186`, `:226-236`). Here the same miss routes secure content to a shared container.

THE BFF'S OWN SAFETY NET IS DOCUMENTED AS THE OPPOSITE OF THIS TASK. `RecordContainerResolver.cs:211-217` says the live assertion "that sprk_issecure is neither field-secured nor NULL on any securable row belongs with task 047", and the ABSENT branch (`:218-225`) only logs a warning and then treats absent as not-secure (`:227`). After this task the column IS field-secured, so that comment is wrong and the warning is the only signal that the app identity lost its FLS Read.

TODAY'S WRITERS (verified 2026-09-30):
- Client create, user context: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateProjectWizard/projectService.ts:280-285` sets `sprk_issecure = true` in the Xrm create payload. Reached from `CreateProjectWizard.tsx` (provisioning after create at `:683-722`) and from `SummarizeFilesWizard/SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx:515-531` (same ProjectService; its own provisioning call and failure copy at `:538-570`, including the "marked Secure but could not be provisioned" branch whose wording stops being true once the client no longer writes the flag).
- BFF: `Api/ExternalAccess/UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:232-238` clears it (app identity). `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:279-284` REQUIRES it already true and does not set it.
- MDA forms of all three roots (live, not in source control) — the only way a matter or work assignment is marked secure today.
- Unknown until inventoried live: business rules, classic workflows, Power Automate flows, data imports.
No matter or work-assignment wizard writes it (grep of src/client for `issecure`, case-insensitive).

THE ORDERING TRAP WHEN THE FLAG MOVES SERVER-SIDE. Today a secure-requested project is born with the flag true, so if provisioning then fails, the wizard's upload step (`CreateProjectWizard.tsx:725-736`) hits `RecordContainerResolver`'s fail-closed branch and uploads nothing. If the client simply stops writing the flag and provisioning fails, the project is born NOT secure and the same upload step puts the files in the shared business-unit container — permanently. The wizard also creates an event (`:625-660`) before provisioning.

THE MIXED-VERSION TRAP. Once IsSecured is on, a create payload that still carries `sprk_issecure` from a user without Create permission on the field is refused — so a cached old client bundle would fail EVERY secure project create. And during rollout, records created by the old client arrive at provisioning already flagged true. Provisioning must therefore accept "already flagged, not yet provisioned" as well as "not flagged", and the FLS import must come after the client that stops writing the flag is deployed. So the server must set the flag as its first mutation, and the client must not upload or create children for a secure-requested record whose provisioning did not succeed.

NO UNSECURE SURFACE EXISTS. `SecureProjectSection.test.tsx:113` records that no client calls `/unsecure-project`; secure matters and work assignments have no secure surface except the form field this task locks. Locking without an endpoint-backed surface would remove a capability.

`sprk_accesspermission` stays editable by Write-holders (owner-accepted, session 27) — out of scope.</background>
