  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every reader of sprk_issecure (BFF app-only, BFF OBO/impersonated, client Xrm.WebApi, PCF). None may be masked. The FLS profile grants Read to every principal that can read the row; a design that leaves any reader masked is rejected even if every write test passes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 2">Scope: writes. After this task the ONLY writer of sprk_issecure is the BFF app identity inside the secure (provision) and unsecure endpoints. The BFF app user(s) are associated with the writer profile explicitly; do not rely on System Administrator bypassing FLS. Under D-13 (per-customer BFF app registration) the association is an environment-setup/pipeline step, not a hard-coded identity. The platform's System Administrator field-security permission (auto-created, full, not narrowable) is the one residual human writer — it is surfaced to the owner (escalation), never silently accepted and never "fixed" by removing the System Administrator role from anyone.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: rollout compatibility. Provisioning accepts both a record that is not yet flagged (the new client) and one already flagged true but not provisioned (the old client, and records created before this task) and treats both identically; an already-provisioned record keeps the existing 409. The live order is: BFF, then client, then the IsSecured import — never IsSecured before the client that stops writing the flag is live.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: the BFF app identity's own read. Its FLS Read on sprk_issecure (all three roots) is a standing, checked invariant (the sibling assertion), not only an operator step — the standing-grant precedent shows an unchecked operator step stays unapplied. The stale `RecordContainerResolver.cs:211-217` comment is rewritten to state the new invariant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the secure-create flow (CreateProjectWizard and SummarizeFilesDialog). The client never writes sprk_issecure. The BFF sets it true as the FIRST mutation of provisioning, verified by read-back. A secure-requested create whose provisioning returns non-success uploads no file and creates no child record in any shared container; the user sees the existing authored provisioning-failure copy (task 068).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the new secure/unsecure surface. It calls task 144's generalized provision/unsecure endpoints only (no new BFF endpoint), is shown on sprk_project, sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment, and relies on the endpoints' delegation filter (Write on the record) for authorization — the client does not decide who may secure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: enforcement. FLS is platform configuration, not a plugin; no plugin is added. Live proof is a MANUAL gate with the existing non-admin test users in their current BU — no Dataverse in CI, no user relocation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / pcf constraints">Scope: any UI touched. Fluent v9 semantic tokens only, dark-mode compliant; mirror the existing `SecureProjectSection.tsx` copy/toggle styling for the secure control rather than inventing a new look.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing bff-extensions.md; publish size against a FRESH master build (short path, same zip tool, both sizes, delta, file counts); at most 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: sprk_accesspermission. Not field-secured, not changed (owner-accepted).</constraint>
  </constraints>

