  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory every writer and reader of sprk_issecure on the three roots: grep src/ (server and client, case-insensitive), plus a live read-only inventory of forms (systemform formxml), business rules, workflows and cloud flows referencing the column. Classify each reader by identity (app-only, OBO, impersonated, client user context). Record in the task note.</step>
    <step order="2">Design the FLS configuration: one profile granting Read to every user (determine the live mechanism that covers all current AND future users — e.g. association with every business unit's default team plus a setup step for new BUs — and verify it on a user in each BU), and one granting Read/Create/Update to the BFF app identity. Record the choice and why in the note.</step>
    <step order="3">Server: provisioning sets sprk_issecure true as its first mutation (read-back verified) instead of requiring it, and accepts an already-flagged, not-yet-provisioned record unchanged (rollout constraint); the unsecure path clears it last (unchanged ordering). Request contract per task 144's generalized DTO. Rewrite the `RecordContainerResolver.cs:211-217` comment and apply the owner's answer on the ABSENT branch. Add the sibling standing assertion (BFF app identity + every BU default team can read; writer set is exactly the expected principals) with seeded unit tests both ways.</step>
    <step order="4">Client: projectService stops writing the flag; CreateProjectWizard and SummarizeFilesDialog pass "secure requested" to provisioning and skip file upload and child creation for a secure-requested record whose provisioning failed.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the endpoint-backed secure/unsecure affordance for project, matter and work assignment (command-bar command via ribbon-edit, or an extension of an existing form control); confirm the choice against the escalation trigger first.</step>
    <step order="6" mode="prescriptive">Live (dev), in order: deploy the BFF; deploy the client changes (and confirm no cached old bundle is still served); create the profiles and their team/user associations (readers, BFF app identity) FIRST; then apply IsSecured on the three columns together with the profiles' field permissions in ONE solution import, so no reader is ever masked (if the platform forces a gap between IsSecured and the field-permission rows, measure it, keep it to one scripted step, and record it); make the form controls read-only; publish; run the sibling assertion by hand and record its output.</step>
    <step order="7">Manual live gate: with an existing non-admin test user, a Web API PATCH and a form edit of sprk_issecure are refused; the same user's Web API read returns the true value on a secure row; the client RecordContainerResolver path for that user resolves a secure record to its own container; secure and unsecure via the new surface work for all three entity types. Record outputs.</step>
    <step order="8">Update the setup guide (FLS profiles, associations, new-BU step) and the schema doc; add the FLS setup (profiles, reader associations incl. the new-BU step, BFF app identity association under D-13) to the same new-environment step task 145 establishes — whichever of 145/150 lands first creates the step, the other extends it; never a second mechanism.</step>
    <step order="9">Build and test (BFF unit/integration, UI component tests), publish-size measurement, TASK-INDEX.md `✅ [done]`, POML status, deviations in the task note.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>No maintainable mechanism grants Read on the secured column to ALL current and future users (the live test shows a user whose read is masked): STOP — do not ship a lock that masks reads. Present the options to the owner (as a CLAUDE.md §6.5 block if the answer bends ADR-003's fail-closed rule). Recommendation: associate the reader profile with every business unit's DEFAULT team (membership is automatic, so every current and future user of an existing BU is covered), make "associate the new BU's default team" part of the new-environment/new-BU step, and have the sibling assertion fail on any BU default team without it — verified live on a user in each BU before step 6's IsSecured import.</trigger>
    <trigger>The live inventory finds a flow, workflow, business rule or integration that writes sprk_issecure as a user: STOP and report it before locking; removing it may break a process the owner relies on.</trigger>
    <trigger>The choice of secure/unsecure surface (command-bar button vs extending an existing control) is a product decision; present a recommendation with a sketch before building if the existing SecureProjectSection pattern cannot be reused on matter and work-assignment forms.</trigger>
    <trigger>WHO may unsecure: the endpoint's delegation filter admits any Write-holder, but the shipped wizard copy (`SecureProjectSection.test.tsx:112-117`) tells users "an administrator can remove the secure designation later". Exposing unsecure to every Write-holder changes that promise; ask the owner whether the surface is shown to Write-holders or restricted (and how), before building it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Removing the secure-requested upload in the failure case changes the wizard's contract in a way the task-068 copy cannot explain (including the SummarizeFilesDialog "marked Secure but could not be provisioned" branch and the CreateProjectWizard "an administrator can secure it" branch): ask for authored copy rather than writing new user-facing wording.</trigger>
    <trigger>OPEN OWNER QUESTION — human System Administrators. Marking the column IsSecured auto-grants the built-in System Administrator field profile full Read/Create/Update, and it cannot be narrowed (teams-app-r1 050 note §2). So "only the BFF writes the flag" holds for every user EXCEPT holders of the System Administrator role, who can still edit it in the form or Web API. Before step 6, put this to the owner. Recommendation: accept it as the platform's administrator boundary (a System Administrator can already reassign, share or delete any secure record), document it in the guide and the schema doc, and have the sibling assertion list every System Administrator holder so the residual writer set is visible — do not strip System Administrator from anyone (it is how the BFF app users hold `prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser`).</trigger>
    <trigger>OPEN OWNER QUESTION — the ABSENT branch. Once the column is secured, `sprk_issecure` absent on a securable row read by the BFF app identity means either a NULL value or a lost FLS Read — and today both route content to the shared container (`RecordContainerResolver.cs:218-227`). Recommendation: backfill NULL to false on the three roots (column default false, verified live), then make ABSENT fail closed (a typed `SdapProblemException`, like `secure_record_container_missing`) so a lost FLS Read refuses uploads instead of mis-routing them. It changes behaviour for every upload path, so ask before step 3's resolver change.</trigger>
    <trigger>Securing an EXISTING record through the new surface before task 148 merges re-owns the root but leaves its existing children (documents, events, to-dos, communications) in ordinary business units and its existing files in the shared container. If step 5 is ready before 148 has merged, ask the owner. Recommendation: ship the lock, the create-time secure path and the unsecure action now, and enable "secure an existing record" in the same release as 148's provisioning transition — or show authored copy that existing content is not moved.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep of src/ for `sprk_issecure` writers: `projectService.ts:283-284` (client create) and `UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:237` (BFF clear). Session 27 live query: 0 `fieldpermission` rows on sprk_issecure. Grep of src/solutions and src/dataverse `*.xml` for `sprk_issecure` returns no FieldSecurityProfile. `SecureProjectSection.test.tsx:113`: no client calls `/unsecure-project`. The ONE existing field-security precedent is `contact.sprk_standinggrant` + the "Standing Grant Administrators" profile (teams-app-r1 050 note; `SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs:168-186`); grep of tests/ for `IsSecured|fieldpermission` returns nothing — no standing check of any FLS configuration exists.</existing>
    <extension>The endpoints are extended (task 144), not added. The FLS profiles are new platform configuration, created with the standing-grant precedent's recipe (050 note §8) rather than a new mechanism; a profile per purpose (reader / BFF writer) is required because the standing-grant profile secures a different column for a different audience. The UI affordance extends an existing surface where one fits (SecureProjectSection pattern / existing form control) and adds a command only if none does. The sibling assertion is new because no FLS check exists and SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion checks roles, not field permissions; it lives beside it at the same KEEP path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any user with Write can clear sprk_issecure on a secure record in the MDA form, bypassing the unsecure endpoint's ownership move and share sweep — the record then reads as non-secure to every container resolver and new content lands in the shared container; any user can also flag a record secure without provisioning, producing a record that 409s every upload.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

