  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Secure flag cannot be changed outside the endpoints (UX amendment (1): no form shows the field)">
      <steps>
        <step>Confirm the recorded live inventory (note section 3.1): no form or view on the four tables references sprk_issecure</step>
        <step>As an existing non-admin test user with Write on a secure matter (outside the "Spaarke Demo" team), PATCH sprk_matters({id}) {"sprk_issecure":false} through the Web API</step>
        <step>As the same user, GET sprk_matters({id})?$select=sprk_issecure</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The PATCH is refused or the value is unchanged on read-back; the read returns true (present, not empty) - the NEGATIVE and NO MASKING gates G-6 / G-7.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Secure and unsecure through the endpoint-backed surface">
      <steps>
        <step>On a non-secure project, matter and work assignment, as a Write-holder (once as the record's creator, once as a Write-holder who did not create it - round 33 item 1), open Access and choose Make Secure; confirm (owner round 27 copy)</step>
        <step>After the refresh, verify the flag reads true and Access now lists Remove Secure, not Make Secure; as the record's creator (the second run), open it - it opens (shared to by the call)</step>
        <step>As the record's creator, choose Remove Secure; confirm (round 33 item 2 copy); after the refresh verify the flag reads false and Access lists Make Secure again</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each action succeeds via the BFF; no console errors; a user without Write sees neither command.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Access group (UX amendment)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_project&amp;id={secure-project-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>As a Write-holder on a SECURE project, open the project form</step>
        <step>Open the Access flyout on the command bar</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Update Access and Remove Secure are listed; Make Secure is not. Every command recorded before the import (Set-AccessRibbon.ps1 before.json) is still on the command bar.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Make Secure (after 148)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_matter&amp;id={non-secure-matter-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>In an environment whose BFF carries task 148 and round 26 item 3's wired file relocation (note section 22.4) and whose ribbon was imported with -SecureTransitionDeployed, as a Write-holder who did NOT create it (round 33 item 1: Make Secure is held to the Write gate) open a NON-secure matter that has a document with a file</step>
        <step>Open Access and choose Make Secure</step>
        <step>Read the confirmation dialog, then choose Make Secure</step>
        <step>Wait for the refresh; read sprk_issecure (Web API) and reopen Access</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The dialog shows exactly the owner round 27 copy: title "Make this matter secure?", the three paragraphs with {record} = matter, buttons "Make Secure" (primary) and "Cancel". After confirming, the record reads secure after the refresh and Access lists Remove Secure, not Make Secure; the matter's creator still opens it (shared to by the call); the document's file is in the matter's own container. If the creator is on the matter's No Access list, an alert after the success notification names them ("... is on this matter's No Access list, so the matter was not shared with them.").</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Make Secure finishes an unfinished transition (round 40 items 1 and 2)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_project&amp;id={project-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Against a LOCAL BFF pointed at dev whose SharePointEmbedded:ContainerTypeId is valid for the type check but whose container creation fails (e.g. a container type the BFF identity cannot create in) - NEVER by changing the shared dev BFF's configuration - as a Write-holder who did NOT create a non-secure project, choose Make Secure and confirm</step>
        <step>Read the failure: a confirm dialog titled "Make Secure" showing the server's container_creation_failed message, buttons "Make Secure" and "Cancel"; choose Cancel</step>
        <step>After the refresh, read sprk_issecure, sprk_containerid and the owner (Web API), then open Access</step>
        <step>Point the local BFF back at a working container type, choose Make Secure on the same record and confirm</step>
        <step>Read sprk_issecure, sprk_containerid, the record's shares (caller and creator) and open Access again</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>After the failure the record reads sprk_issecure = true, owned by the Secure Record owner team, no container; Access lists Make Secure AND Remove Secure. The retry succeeds: its own container is recorded, the record's creator holds the creator's level (Collaborate), the caller holds Collaborate — or Full Access when they held Full Access (Write and Delete) before the call, through a share, through owning the record, or through a security role (round 46 item 1) — and Access then lists Remove Secure and not Make Secure (acceptance (e) as amended: hidden on a PROVISIONED secure record). No console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Make Secure finishes a secure record the Secure Record Owners team does not own (round 46 item 4; the verifier's item 8; round 53 item 2)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_project&amp;id={project-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>In dev, with a BFF carrying rounds 46 and 53 and access_ribbon.js 1.5.0: find a secure project that records its own container and is still owned by a USER (a legacy record provisioned before task 133's owner move — the G-11 check of acceptance (e) for legacy data); and a secure project with its own container that an administrator has reassigned in the model-driven app to an ordinary owner team in ANOTHER business unit (a reassignment outside Spaarke). Read sprk_issecure, sprk_containerid and the owner of each (Web API)</step>
        <step>As a Write-holder, open each and open Access</step>
        <step>Choose Make Secure, confirm; after the refresh read sprk_issecure, sprk_containerid, the owner and the shares (caller and creator), and open Access again</step>
        <step>Open a PROVISIONED secure project (owned by the Secure Record Owners team, its own container) and open Access</step>
        <step>Round 53 item 2: take a secure TEST project created for this ui-test (its own container recorded) and, as a System Administrator in the model-driven app, Assign it to the Secure Record business unit's DEFAULT team (another team INSIDE that business unit — the retired default team's shape); as a Write-holder open it and open Access; then call provisioning on it through the API with transition "make-secure" and read the response; finally run scripts/Migrate-SecureRecordsToNamedOwnerTeam.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl … (dry run, then -Apply -AcceptedAssignCascade as the dry run reports, then -Verify) so it ends on the named team</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>On both unfinished projects Access lists Make Secure AND Remove Secure. After Make Secure each is owned by the Secure Record Owners team, its sprk_containerid is unchanged (the same container, no second one), the caller and the creator are shared (round 46 item 1's levels), and Access lists Remove Secure and not Make Secure. The provisioned project lists Remove Secure and not Make Secure. The project the default team owns lists Remove Secure and NOT Make Secure (it is isolated already; the console shows the "isolated already" note, not a warning); the API call answers 409 sdap.provision.owned_by_other_secure_team naming scripts/Migrate-SecureRecordsToNamedOwnerTeam.ps1 and changes nothing; after the migration's -Verify (exit 0) it is owned by the Secure Record Owners team. No console errors; a "Who owns this record could not be told" warning appears only if the owner answer failed (then Make Secure is hidden on that record).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Make Secure run by the record's OWNER keeps their Full Access (round 46 item 1; round 53 item 3; the verifier's item 6)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_project&amp;id={non-secure-project-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>In dev, with a BFF carrying round 46 and access_ribbon.js 1.5.0: pick a non-admin user whose security role grants Delete on sprk_project at USER (basic) depth only, and a NON-secure project that user OWNS (Assign it to them if needed) but did not create, with no explicit share to them (Manage Access lists none). Record the user's role and its Delete depth</step>
        <step>Before the call, read that user's effective rights on the project as Dataverse reports them: GET {org}/api/data/v9.2/systemusers({user-id})/Microsoft.Dynamics.CRM.RetrievePrincipalAccess(Target=@t)?@t={"@odata.id":"sprk_projects({non-secure-project-id})"}</step>
        <step>As that user, open the project, open Access, choose Make Secure and confirm</step>
        <step>After the refresh, read the owner (Web API) and the project's explicit shares (GET {org}/api/data/v9.2/principalobjectaccessset?$filter=objectid eq {non-secure-project-id}) and open Access again</step>
        <step>As the same user, choose Remove Secure and confirm (F3 check), then read sprk_issecure</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Before the call the user holds Write and Delete (by ownership: no share and no deeper role). After Make Secure the project is owned by the Secure Record Owners team and the user holds an explicit share of Full Access — Read, Write, Append, AppendTo, Share and Delete (accessrightsmask 327703), never Assign — so they still open it and Access lists Remove Secure, not Make Secure; the creator holds Collaborate (262167). Remove Secure then succeeds for them (F3: a Full Access holder) and sprk_issecure reads false. No console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Make Secure run by an ADMINISTRATOR keeps their Full Access (round 46 item 1; round 53 item 3; the verifier's item 6)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_matter&amp;id={non-secure-matter-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>In dev, with a BFF carrying round 46 and access_ribbon.js 1.5.0: as a System Administrator who neither owns nor created a NON-secure matter and holds no explicit share on it, read their effective rights on it (RetrievePrincipalAccess, as in the owner ui-test)</step>
        <step>Open the matter, open Access, choose Make Secure and confirm</step>
        <step>After the refresh, read the owner and the matter's explicit shares (principalobjectaccess) and open Access again</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Before the call the administrator holds Write and Delete through their role (no share, not the owner). After Make Secure the matter is owned by the Secure Record Owners team; the administrator holds an explicit Full Access share (accessrightsmask 327703 — Delete kept, never Assign), shared like any caller of the command (round 46 item 3); the matter's creator holds Collaborate (262167). Access lists Remove Secure, not Make Secure. No console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="F3 refusal">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_matter&amp;id={secure-matter-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>As a Collaborate holder who is NOT the record's creator (and not a Full Access holder), open a SECURE matter</step>
        <step>Open Access and choose Remove Secure; read the confirmation dialog, then choose Remove Secure</step>
        <step>Read sprk_issecure (Web API) after the refresh</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The dialog shows exactly the round 33 copy: title "Remove the secure designation from this matter?", its two paragraphs with {record} = matter, buttons "Remove Secure" (primary) and "Cancel". Then an alert titled "Remove Secure" shows the endpoint's refusal message (sdap.unsecure.not_permitted ProblemDetails detail, verbatim); the record stays secure. Repeated by the creator and by a Full Access holder: both succeed.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Read-only user">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_workassignment&amp;id={work-assignment-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>As a user with Read but not Write, open a SECURE work assignment and open Access (if shown)</step>
        <step>Repeat on a NON-secure work assignment</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>On both records neither Make Secure nor Remove Secure is available (the Access flyout itself is hidden for a caller with no Access command).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Secure create with failed provisioning uploads nothing">
      <steps>
        <step>Run the Create Project wizard with Secure on and a file attached, with provisioning forced to fail — against a locally-run BFF pointed at dev with a misconfigured `SecureRecord:OwnerTeamName`, NEVER by changing the shared dev BFF's configuration</step>
        <step>Finish the wizard</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The task-068 provisioning-failure copy is shown; no sprk_document row exists for the file and no file exists in any shared container.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode</step>
        <step>Verify the secure affordance and any changed wizard copy adapt (no hard-coded colours)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours use Fluent v9 semantic tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_issecure is IsSecured on sprk_project, sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment in dev; the reader profile covers every existing user (verified on a user in each business unit) and the setup covers future users/BUs; the BFF app identity is explicitly associated with the writer profile.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE, NEGATIVE: an existing non-admin test user with Write on a record cannot change sprk_issecure via Web API PATCH, via the MDA form, or via a create payload on any of the three roots — each attempt is refused or the value is unchanged on read-back.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE, NO MASKING: the same user's Web API read of a secure row returns sprk_issecure = true (present, not absent); the client RecordContainerResolver.ts path as that user resolves the secure record to its own container, not a fallback; the BFF RecordContainerResolver logs no "ABSENT (not false)" warning for it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file under src/client writes sprk_issecure; projectService.test.ts asserts the create payload has no sprk_issecure key when secure is requested.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Provisioning sets the flag true as its first mutation, verified by read-back; a record already flagged true but not provisioned is provisioned exactly like an unflagged one; a record that is already secure and provisioned still returns the existing 409.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE, BFF READ: the sibling assertion, run by hand against dev, passes (BFF app identity and every BU default team can read sprk_issecure on all three roots; the writer set is exactly the BFF app identity's profile plus the System Administrator profile) and FAILS when seeded with a census lacking the BFF read or listing an extra writer (unit tests both ways); outputs recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`RecordContainerResolver.cs`'s ABSENT-branch comment states the new invariant, and the ABSENT branch behaves as the owner decided under the escalation trigger (with a test for the chosen behaviour).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The owner's rulings on the System Administrator residual writer, the ABSENT branch, who may unsecure, and securing existing records before task 148 are recorded in the task note, and the shipped behaviour matches them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a secure-requested create whose provisioning fails leaves no uploaded file and no child sprk_document/event in any container (both wizard paths), and shows the existing failure copy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AUTHORIZATION: a caller without Write on the record is refused by the secure and unsecure endpoints (403) for all three entity types; nothing changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Users can secure and unsecure a project, matter and work assignment through the new endpoint-backed surface (manual live gate, recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The live writer inventory (forms, business rules, workflows, flows) is recorded in the task note with each writer's disposition.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_accesspermission is unchanged (not field-secured).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Setup guide and pipeline/runbook step carry the FLS profiles and associations; the schema doc states the field is secured and who may write it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF unit/integration and UI component suites green; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 and at most 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the stated contract plus the negative, masking and authorization cases above. Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the note.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner round 2 item 2 and live fact "0 fieldpermission rows" (session27 note). Relates to defect C10 (session26 note): the flag is the label that drives container placement and the evaluator's Secure suppression, so a user-writable flag undoes both. Depends on task 144 (generalized endpoints). Task 145 establishes the pipeline/runbook step that the FLS setup joins. Task 148 (transitions) edits the same endpoints and makes "secure an existing record" carry its children; task 151 edits RecordContainerResolver.cs first. Precedent: teams-app-r1 task 050/051 (contact.sprk_standinggrant FLS; the BFF read grant that was never applied). #1037 (show a secure record disabled with the reason) is word-add-in-r1's and unaffected.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in knowledge before starting. Step 6 is prescriptive; the BFF and client ship together (the client stops writing the flag in the same release the server starts setting it).</protocol>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-150" result="partial">
      <summary>Code, scripts, tests and docs complete; no live write performed (every live step is a pending manual gate, in order G-0 to G-10, notes/task-150-issecure-lock.md section 9). Step 5 ribbon STOPPED: task 142's Access group has not merged (UX amendment sequencing trigger). Merge gate: owner picks the F6 draft copy (note section 6).</summary>
      <done>
        - Server: ProvisionProjectEndpoint sets sprk_issecure as its FIRST write (read back; new reason sdap.provision.secure_flag_not_set), accepts unflagged and already-flagged records identically, keeps the 409; UnsecureProjectEndpoint enforces F3 (Full Access = Write + Delete, or the creator via createdby / sprk_createdbyperson; 403 sdap.unsecure.not_permitted) and refuses an EMPTY flag; RecordContainerResolver refuses an ABSENT flag on the record and on every root above it (secure_flag_unreadable 503) - the owner's ABSENT-branch decision.
        - Client: projectService never writes the flag; CreateProjectWizard provisions FIRST and adds no file, document record, work assignment, event or email to a secure-requested project whose provisioning did not succeed; copy updated (DRAFT, F6).
        - Scripts (dry-run default, -Apply, -Verify; only dry runs executed, read-only): scripts/Repair-SecureFlagNulls.ps1 (Q1; covers every carrier of the column, incl. sprk_invoice found in review), scripts/Set-SecureFlagFieldSecurity.ps1 (reuses task 133's two profiles; refuses -Apply without them, every default team, exact writer membership, NULL cleanup and -ClientNoLongerWritesFlag).
        - Standing assertion SecureFlagFieldSecurityAssertion (tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl) with 14 perturbations, script-agreement pins and an opt-in live census (run read-only against dev: FAIL 5 = correct pre-lock verdict).
        - Docs: guide section 7c (+ table row, section 8 rows, related), schema doc corrected (no business rule exists live), 145 handoff extended (S10-S15), scripts/README.md.
      </done>
      <live-inventory>No form, view, business rule, classic workflow, cloud flow or Spaarke plugin references sprk_issecure (escalation trigger 2 did not fire). Reader-profile-on-every-default-team mechanism proven live by task 141's profile (6 of 6) - escalation trigger 1 did not fire. NULL rows: 9 projects, 18 matters, 11 work assignments, 4 invoices; all root NULLs predate the column.</live-inventory>
      <owner-rulings>F3, F4, F6, F7, ABSENT branch, Q1, R5, R6 applied as recorded in the note section 2; none newly asked.</owner-rulings>
      <placement>Extends two existing endpoints and one existing resolver: no new endpoint, service, DI registration, option, job, package or column (bff-extensions.md: modification of existing surface). FLS is platform configuration, no plugin (ADR-002).</placement>
      <justification-new-items>
        - Reason codes (4 new): existing reasonCode contracts, extended; without them the client cannot tell "could not mark secure" / "not allowed to unsecure" / "masked flag" apart.
        - Repair-SecureFlagNulls.ps1: no NULL backfill exists (grep scripts/); without it the ABSENT refusal refuses every upload to the 42 pre-column rows.
        - Set-SecureFlagFieldSecurity.ps1: Set-RecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 owns the profiles and is reused, not forked; without the lock every Write holder can change the flag (the defect).
        - SecureFlagFieldSecurityAssertion: SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion checks roles, not field permissions, and no FLS check exists (grep tests/ for fieldpermission); without it the BFF's FLS Read stays an unchecked operator step (the standing-grant precedent).
        - describeHeldBackForSecure (client helper): none exists; without it the user is not told why the files and children they asked for are missing.
      </justification-new-items>
      <stops>Ribbon Make Secure / Remove Secure (amendment acceptance a-f and its UI tests) - waits for task 142's group; Make Secure additionally waits for 148 (F7) and owner-authored confirmation copy.</stops>
      <residuals>Other app-only readers (ExternalParticipationService FR-22 suppression, ExternalDataService, InternalShareEndpoints, ExternalGrantLifecycle, SubjectStandingGrantReader, RecordOwnershipResolver) still map an EMPTY flag to not secure - unmasked by the writer membership, guarded by the assertion; sprk_invoice.sprk_issecure exists and is not locked (owner question); the provision API accepts an existing non-secure record (unchanged capability; F7 gates the surface).</residuals>
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-150-r1" result="partial" round="verifier r1">
      <summary>Adversarial verifier round 1 (25 items). Items 1-7 were verifications (no change). Items 8, 9 and 25 fixed (comments now match code). Item 10 recorded as an F6 input with a resume-neutral option D and the client comment corrected; the DRAFT copy is unchanged pending the owner. Item 11 made a merge gate (G-0 in dev before master) in the note, the guide section 7c and the 145 handoff. Item 12 made a merge gate (133 first or together). Item 13 raised as an OWNER QUESTION (not implemented). Item 14 recorded as a handoff to 146 and the route-sweep row 67 fix. Item 15: the lock script retries a refused PUT once with the Boolean cast and the OptionSet expanded; the dry run (read-only) confirmed all three columns are BooleanAttributeMetadata. Items 16-24 stay open: live gates, the 142/148 stops and the main session's publish-size and CVE checks. No live write.</summary>
      <done>
        - Item 8: UnsecureProjectEndpoint.RefuseUnlessPermittedToRemoveAsync remarks now say an unestablished caller identity refuses 403 sdap.unsecure.permission_unverifiable and an unreadable creator person refuses 500 (same reason key, retryable), matching the code and SecureProjectShareTests.
        - Item 9: ProvisionProjectEndpoint Step 1 heading now says it confirms only that the record exists (the flag is set later).
        - Item 10: provisioningService.ts comment on the environment-refusal branch states the RESUME case (the record is already flagged, and team-owned on a resume); note section 6 adds option D (resume-neutral) for row 2. Copy unchanged: F6 is the owner's.
        - Item 11: G-0 (Repair-SecureFlagNulls.ps1 -Apply then -Verify) must run in dev before task 150 merges to master, and in every other environment before it receives this BFF; recorded in note section 9 (G-0 row + merge gates), guide section 7c step 0 and handoff S13. No deploy script enforces it; -Verify exit 0 is the gate.
        - Item 12: merge gate - task/uac-r2-133-b2-r2 merges first or together (F3 trusts sprk_createdbyperson, safe only under 133's FLS).
        - Item 13: OWNER QUESTION in note section 11.6 with options (a) accept until 148, (b) creator-only for an UNFLAGGED record (recommended), (c) recently-created only. Not implemented.
        - Item 14: handoff in note section 11.7 - field-mappings/push (route sweep row 67) and task 146's app-identity AI creates must deny sprk_issecure and sprk_createdbyperson as target columns.
        - Item 15: Set-SecureFlagFieldSecurity.ps1 - on a refused PUT of a BooleanAttributeMetadata, retry ONCE with the cast and $expand=OptionSet; any other type or a second refusal throws; the dry run prints the attribute type. Parse check 0 errors; dry run against spaarkedev1 (read-only) printed #Microsoft.Dynamics.CRM.BooleanAttributeMetadata for all three tables. Unproven live until G-4.
        - #1081 peer report: G-6 must use a user outside the "Spaarke Demo" team (System Administrator via team; the dry run lists it); recorded in note sections 9 and 11.8.
      </done>
      <placement>No new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job, column or package. Changes are comments, docs and an operator-script retry branch inside the existing lock step.</placement>
      <merge-gates>(1) owner F6 copy pick, (2) G-0 run in dev first, (3) task 133 merged first or together.</merge-gates>
      <open>Item 13 owner question; items 16-24: publish size + CVE (main session), live gates G-3/G-4/G-5/G-6/G-7/G-8, ribbon surface (task 142) and Make Secure (task 148, owner copy), F6 copy, and pre-existing UI jest failures in untouched suites (confirmed on the work branch by the verifier).</open>
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-150-r2" result="partial" round="verifier r2">
      <summary>Adversarial verifier round 2 (16 items). F1-F6 closed: the first-write criterion is now pinned against the Step 4.2 shared-container unlink (the verifier's own reorder seed fails 4 new tests); two stale resolver comments reworded; the lock script reverts IsSecured when a grant fails after securing, prints a recovery banner when the revert fails too, and re-running -Apply now grants what is missing on an already-secured column; the schema doc states the FLS configuration as the target pending G-4; configured writers (field-mapping rules, AI topic registry, email update fields) are a standing check (lock script p6, assertion clause 5; 0 live); a throwing Full Access probe refuses with a reason code. Items 9-16 stay open (live gates, 142/148 stop, publish size + CVE, merge gates, owner question). No live write.</summary>
      <done>
        - F1: SecureFlagEndpointWriteTests +4 - Provision_ARecordCarryingASharedContainer_SetsTheFlagBeforeUnlinkingIt (business-unit and configured shared container; the sprk_issecure write's Sequence precedes the sprk_containerid = null write) and ..._WhenTheFlagWriteIsRefused_NeverUnlinksIt (SecureFlagWriteFails: no unlink attempted, link kept, owner unchanged, no grant, no container). Seed S13 (flag write moved after the unlink, just before wroteCreatorShare) fails all 4.
        - F2: RecordContainerResolver.cs co-mingle query comment and the not-found predicate remarks now name the secure_flag_unreadable refusal (task 150), not the retired absent-flag warning. Comment-only.
        - F3: Set-SecureFlagFieldSecurity.ps1 - the PUT is factored into Set-ColumnSecured; a grant failure after it reverts IsSecured on that table, publishes and reads it back, then rethrows; a failed revert prints "!!! RECOVERY REQUIRED NOW" with two remedies; on an already-secured column -Apply grants only the missing permissions (the resume path; it used to skip the table). Header STEPS (b) documents it. Exercised by an offline harness (az and Invoke-RestMethod shadowed): revert OK, revert fails, resume, configured writer; the r1 script under the same harness leaves the table secured and ungranted and does not grant on resume.
        - F4: secure-project-fields-schema.md - column row, Field Security row, correction paragraph and form note state the configuration as the TARGET, pending G-3/G-4 (live 2026-10-03: IsSecured=false, 0 fieldpermission rows).
        - F5: adopted and widened - note section 3.1 row; lock script precondition (p6); standing assertion clause 5 (census ConfiguredWriters, channels sprk_fieldmappingrule.sprk_targetfield, sprk_aitopicregistry.sprk_targetfield, sprk_emailupdatefield.sprk_targetfieldlogicalname; entity sets resolved live) with 4 tests; seed S15 (clause disabled) fails 3. Live read-only: 0 rows on all three (25 field-mapping rules in total); the lock script's dry run against spaarkedev1 reports OK (p6), zero writes.
        - F6: UnsecureProjectEndpoint.RefuseUnlessPermittedToRemoveAsync wraps GetCallerRightsAsync; a throw other than this request's cancellation refuses 500 sdap.unsecure.permission_unverifiable before any write. Fixture switch FullAccessProbeThrows (throws on a record's second probe; the first is the route's Write gate); test Unsecure_WhenTheFullAccessCheckThrows_RefusesWithAReasonBeforeAnyWrite; seed S14 (catch disabled) fails it.
