      <interpretation>Round 53 item 1's verbatim copy and the wizard client's binding copy rule (task 068/133, FR-31: "never advise trying again in the message", pinned for every code) meet in one clause. The server and the ribbon carry the ratified sentence whole; the wizard's message is that sentence with {record} = project and without its closing "; you may try again", because in that client the retry is the host's action keyed on retryable: true ("Try securing again") - the same promise as an action, never as words. The wizards never receive this code. Note section 25.1.</interpretation>
